hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1512","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One night, while sleeping, I saw in a dream as if we were in the house of Uqbah bin Rafi', and fresh dates were brought before us, which are called the dates of Ibn Tab. I interpreted this as meaning that our rank will be elevated in this world, we will have a good end in the Hereafter, and surely our religion is better and excellent."
"1513","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: I saw in a dream that I was migrating from Makkah to a land where there are date-palm trees. My assumption went towards Yamamah and Hajar, but it turned out to be Madinah, whose name is also Yathrib. And in that same dream, I saw that I shook a sword and it broke from the top. Its interpretation turned out to be the defeat of the Muslims on the day of Uhud. Then I shook the sword a second time and it became as strong and good as before from the front. Its interpretation was that Allah the Exalted granted victory and the group of Muslims was established (meaning after the battle of Uhud, Khaybar and Makkah were conquered and the army of Islam gained strength). And in that same dream, I saw cows (that were being slaughtered), and Allah the Exalted is better (as this phrase is said: Allah is better). By this were meant those Muslims who were martyred at Uhud, and by ""goodness"" was meant the goodness that Allah the Exalted sent after that, and the reward of truthfulness that Allah the Exalted granted us after Badr."
"1514","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` Musaylimah the Liar (who falsely claimed prophethood and for this reason was given the title ""the Liar""; after the death of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, he was killed along with his followers) came to Madinah during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: ""If Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) gives me succession after him, I will follow him."" Musaylimah the Liar had brought many people from his tribe with him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came to him, and with him was Thabit bin Qais bin Shamas (may Allah be pleased with him), and in the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was a piece of wood. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, stood among the people of Musaylimah and said: ""O Musaylimah! Even if you ask me for this piece of wood, I would not give it to you, and I am not going to decide about you against the command of Allah. And if you do not accept what I say, Allah the Exalted will kill you."" (This statement of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came true.) ""And indeed, I know you as the one about whom I was shown in a dream, and Thabit will answer you on my behalf."" Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, left from there. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I asked people, ""What did the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, mean by saying: 'You are the one shown to me in a dream about you'?"" So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I was sleeping when I saw (in a dream) two gold bangles in my hand. They seemed evil to me, and in the dream it was inspired to me to blow on them, so I blew and both of them flew away. I interpreted it as two liars who will appear after me. One of them is the 'Anasi from Sana'a and the other is the Yamamah one (Musaylimah the Liar)."
"1515","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""Whoever sees me in a dream will soon see me while awake, or he said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me while awake. Satan cannot take my form."" Abu Salamah said that Abu Qatadah said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has seen me has seen the truth."
"1516","Abu Salamah says: I heard from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: A good dream is from Allah Almighty and a bad dream is from Satan. So when any of you sees a disliked dream, he should spit to his left side or (without spitting) blow lightly and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, then that dream will not harm him. Abu Salamah said: I used to see some dreams that were heavier upon me than a mountain, but when I heard this hadith, I no longer cared about them."
"1517","Abu Salamah says: I used to see such dreams that (because of fear of them) I would fall ill. Then I met Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) (and asked him about this). He said that I was also in the same condition, until I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""A good dream is from Allah, so when any of you sees a good dream, he should not relate it except to his friend. And when he sees a bad dream, he should spit three times to his left and seek refuge with Allah from the evil of Satan, and he should not relate it to anyone, then it will not harm him."
"1518","`Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any of you sees a dream which he dislikes, he should spit three times to his left and seek Allah’s protection from Satan three times, and turn to the other side from which he was lying."
"1519","`Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The dream of a believer is one part out of forty-six parts of prophethood. (That is, there are forty-six important things in prophethood, and one of them is a true dream.)"
"1520","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: When the Day of Judgment draws near, a Muslim’s dream will not be false, and the truest dream among you will be of the one who is most truthful in speech. And a Muslim’s dream is one part out of forty-five parts of Prophethood. And dreams are of three types: one is a good dream which is glad tidings from Allah Almighty, the second is a distressing dream which is from Satan, and the third is a dream which is a thought from one’s own heart. So when any of you sees a bad dream, he should stand up and offer prayer and not mention it to people. And I consider seeing chains on the feet in a dream to be good, and a collar around the neck to be bad. The narrator (Ayyub) said: I do not know whether this statement is part of the hadith or the words of Ibn Sirin."
"1521","‘Ubaydullah bin ‘Abdullah bin ‘Utbah narrates that Sayyiduna ‘Abdullah bin ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) used to say that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I saw in a dream at night that pieces of cloud were dripping with ghee and honey, and people were collecting it with their palms, some taking more and some less. And I saw that a rope was hanging from the sky to the earth, you (peace and blessings be upon him) held it and ascended. Then after you, a man held it and he also ascended. Then another man held it and he also ascended. Then another man held it, but it broke, then it was joined again and he also ascended.” Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah! May my father be sacrificed for you, allow me to interpret it.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Alright, interpret it.” Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “The piece of cloud is Islam, and the ghee and honey refer to the sweetness and gentleness of the Qur’an, and the people who take more or less are those who have memorized more or less of the Qur’an. And the rope hanging from the sky to the earth is the true religion upon which you (peace and blessings be upon him) are. Then Allah will call you to Himself upon this religion. After you, another person (your successor) will hold it and ascend in the same way, then another person will hold it and the same will happen to him. Then another person will hold it, and there will be some disturbance, but that disturbance will eventually be removed and he will also ascend. O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, tell me, have I interpreted it correctly?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “You have interpreted some correctly and some incorrectly.” Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah! Please tell me what mistake I made?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Do not swear.”"
"1522","‘Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that’ a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I saw in a dream that my head was cut off, it kept rolling away and I was running after it.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Do not relate (such a dream) to people, for it is something with which Satan plays with you in your dream.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said that after this, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say in a sermon, “None of you should relate that which Satan plays with him in his dream.”"
